      "number": 2,
      "title": "The Good Giver",
      "content": "The miracles we are seeking are going to come from God... Not our desires.\n\nCreating a miracle happens everyday... or it should.\n\nThere is a miracle every single time you overcome the urge to go to that website, not because you're over hot girls... but because God wants better from you.\n\nRemember, the hope, the motion and the emotion comes from the motive.\n\nThe one the father sets free is free indeed. If you're 'hoping' that something other than the Word of God will give you the right miracle, you might keep searching until you find the narrow path.\n\nThe Word is meant to activate the part of us that needs the supernatural. We hear miracles and think about raising someone from eternal slumber.\nThere is a miracle every time a man decides to call his wife rather than that girl... because he wants to be a man of God.\n\nDon't forget the cause.\nThe intention of a person is everything that's why effort should be rewarded. When you notice effort, you're witnessing the tangible essence of hope.\nBut the full fruit that comes from that sprout will come through action... but that activating force must be directed from God in order to see a miracle!\n\nWe act in obedience to His word. Read it, pray with it and bathe in it!\nWe use our hands and feet and do whatever it takes to reach the ones who need to hear about love the most. It's always easy to preach to the choir!\n\nWe must serve others... As the world turns and people lose hope, there are less and less people manifesting the power of gifting.\nThis is important because it's the fastest eroding pillar of the faith.\n\nRomans 12:6-8\n\"Having then gifts differing according to the grace that is given to us, whether prophecy, let us prophesy according to the proportion of faith; Or ministry, let us wait on our ministering: or he that teacheth, on teaching; Or he that exhorteth, on exhortation: he that giveth, let him do it with simplicity; he that ruleth, with diligence; he that sheweth mercy, with cheerfulness.\"\n\nBeing a Good Giver is one of the greatest gifts and these are some of the greatest miracle-workers!\n\nAll good things come from God. But for God to do anything, He will use a man such as Adam. We are all just like Adam until we become like Jesus (he was the \"the similitude of Adam's transgression, who is the figure of him that was to come.\" Romans 5:14)\n\nWe get life - eternally - because he gave his life... and forgave us...\nFor-giving is how to use forgiveness.\nForgiving someone is the greatest miracle that makes all other miracles possible.\n\nYes... it's a miracle because some of the things God and the Holy Spirit will ask you to forgive and turn the other cheek will seem unforgivable, heinous or just atrocious. And that's why it's a miracle.\n\nFind out where it is in your heart where you're harboring unforgiveness.\nMatthew 5:23-24\n\"Therefore if thou bring thy gift to the altar, and there rememberest that thy brother hath ought against thee; Leave there thy gift before the altar, and go thy way; first be reconciled to thy brother, and then come and offer thy gift.\"\n\nForgiveness is a cycle started by God through Jesus and empowered by the Holy Spirit. We forgive just as we are forgiven. There's a loop of giving forgotten forgiveness that will unlock a realm of miracles, blessings and favor.\n\nMatthew 6:14-15\n\"For if ye forgive men their trespasses, your heavenly Father will also forgive you: But if ye forgive not men their trespasses, neither will your Father forgive your trespasses.\"",
