      "number": 3,
      "title": "Don't forget to give...",
      "content": "Anything and everything we get is for giving... don't forget to give.\nIt's like a spiritual cypher for a good life and many miracles.\n\nMiracles are results that manifest into reality. The spiritual definition is 'faith'.\n\nMiracles are acts of faith and all these things only happen when God allows. Being in alignment with God is the foundation of everything that follows.\n\nThe first psalm blesses the man who walks \"not in the counsel of the ungodly, nor stands in the way of sinners.\"\nThis means you must be aligned with the right people.\n\nThe good giver is one that's already forgiven.\nThe good giver understands principles, knowledge, wisdom, insight.... counsel, discretion and all the other attributes of righteousness.\n\nThe principle of righteousness is the theme of the Bible. God is the ultimate giver. He's the only one who knows what to give... He's the one who even gave us the gift of giving.\n\nIt is important to exercise the gift of gifting in tandem with discernment. When we give, we are sowing seed. It is up to us to determine where we're sowing our seed.\n\nThe seeds are words... or attention we give the words we see, hear and think about.\n\nBeing able to seek and see miracles means giving your attention to the things that give more growth. It's a principle in action. If you give your gift more attention, that gift will give you more to pay attention to.\n\nThe good giver is able to discern how to use their time and also how and where to give.\n\nAdam and Jesus were given all the powers of the Holy Spirit because they are flesh.\n\nIt is true, in this world, God is going to place his gifts in people of flesh and bones. It is up to our prayers and motives to be aligned with these people to access these gifts that are in people by the guidance of the Holy Spirit we have access to the personhood of Jesus even if he's not here in flesh.\n\nOur focus hence tends to the Holy Spirit and how we interact with him. We already expressed the need for knowledge.\nThere is also this need for alignment that's empowered by forgiveness. This will make a man of flesh of bone be able to do the supernatural things through access and fellowship with the source... the Holy Spirit of God.\n\nJohn 14:26 – \"But the Comforter, which is the Holy Ghost, whom the Father will send in my name, he shall teach you all things, and bring all things to your remembrance, whatsoever I have said unto you.\"\n\nWe can't underestimate the depth and scope of the things that need to come to our remembrance.\nIt is important to be rooted and grounded in the knowledge of the ancestors as The Bible is Amazing expounds on in great detail.\n\nThe Holy Spirit gives us ancient and future teachings within the moment. AI systems try to model this spiritual science through technology but the Bible gives us access to the user manual and the Holy Spirit teaches us... page-by-page.\n\nActs 2:38 – \"Then Peter said unto them, Repent, and be baptized every one of you in the name of Jesus Christ for the remission of sins, and ye shall receive the gift of the Holy Ghost.\"\n\nAccess to the Holy Spirit is not a physical reactive process but a spiritually activated channel that starts with baptism. This act, which can be done at any moment, symbolizes cleansing, renewal and rebirth. It brings a person's spirit into a rebirth of a different genealogy that's linked to their physical ancestors through the Bible.\n\nBeing baptized is important but it's more important to be born again in your heart... Even if you haven't done the physical act of bathing in the Spirit, you can receive the Spirit of God at any moment in time...\nThat's the eternal, abundant gift of grace... It's not Neuralink or SpaceX, it's more practical, sustainable and realistic.\n\nSince we have been given the Holy Spirit and his abundance, we are also required to give from what we receive.\n\nThe original Church acted on this abundant 'giving principle'.\nThey gave all they had to each other and everyone was rich.\n\nWe live in a world of poverty because the main principle is to take... take as much as you can... make more than you need and give nothing...\n\nWe give thanks and praise.\nWe give unto God what is His...\nHe gave us life and what do we give him in return?\n\nWhat do you feel you are giving God?\n\nThat void of what you feel you are able and capable of giving and what God actually gave you is where the miracle starts...\nIt was the small faith that was needed... it was there, but it was small...\nIt was two fish and five loaves... it was small... but that was all that was necessary!\n\nWhat is the small thing in which you can give God your all?",
      "wordCount": 839,
      "image": "",
