      "body": "I lost a friend, I lost a fiend,\nI lost a lover, I lost an enemy,\nA slithering serpentine silver-tounged seducer,\nI fell into a puff of smoke, intoxicated by the life we'd make, I lost a foe, I lost a ghost.\n\nHer eyes were the first whiff of ecstasy my soul has ever known, Her smile decorated by those perforating lips were like a sweet taste of the galaxy,\nOur hearts beating at once as one, were like a universe under our skins,\nLost in the twist of the orbital spin, the world has a tilt so my love is biased for you!\nI lost a lover, I lost a ghost.\n\nWe'd talk, we'd imagine a future free of the past, a world made of present declarations,\nI thought the wounds we bravely faced were our preparation, I thought our devotion was our reparation,\nBut under observation, you caused deeper scars and wounds than I'd ever felt,\nYou opened a hole in my soul I was scared had never left, Unjustly taking my faith, mobbing my sanity; my heart felt that theft,\nI lost a friend, I lost a ghost.\n\nIntimate, our bodies static under the stars of the planet, Palms placed in each other's arms as we mould into an embrace,\nI never thought we could stop or we'd have to hit the emergency brakes,\nI can never look at your face without feeling like strangling you,\n\nYour lies pierced my soul because against all odds,\nI still trusted you and thought you were true,\nI told you things about my past that no one knew, and you shared the same with me too,\n\nBut after a single lie is told, all you've ever uttered turns to dust and is under the scrutiny of doubt,\nI can't believe you planted the seeds of deceit between you and me!\n\nI lost a lover, I lost a friend,\nI'll love another, if I can love again,\nBut what's in my heart is forever changed, I lost a lover, I lost a ghost.",
