      "title": "DANCING IN THE RAIN",
      "body": "Still dancing in the dark,\nTattooed the booze to my liver, it looks like a stain,\nFeed my feet when I hurl the free food I found in a black trash bag.\n\nAre we going to build the pyramids again?\nTime can't stop drop and roll when I'm burning with passion for change,\nI won the race, consoled by loneliness, None beyond the finish line, it lonely at the t-\n\nI lost the old me,\nA silent night, a lonely heart,\nA single tear extinguishing the burning candle, on a stale cupcake for my birthday...\nWhere's the love?\nI need you near dear, come here and whisper in my ear.\n\nI learnt patience when I was waiting for you, but it was well worth the pain.\n\nToday is a state I couldn't even contemplate all those days when I'd sleep with a pillow drenched in tears from muffled cries under a moonless night.\n\nI trust my heart, I trust your love…",
