      "id": "p053",
      "collection": "Spoken Word",
      "title": "Homiletics",
      "body": "The song sings to my heart The words sting my soul.\nA touch shatters her fragile frame in my palms.\nAll seems to come undone when I flicker my tongue.\n\nSince we're young,\nI thought the stars and all the distant suns were just for us,\nI thought we're made for fun, but it seems we rushed too much.\n\nWe're searching for the sparkles when our eyes meet.\nHow could this cloud of love ever delete or face defeat?\nMy heart may be weak but my soul's elastic.\n\nTime continues to another dimension.\nI can't find the right words to illustrate how my heart works. The world is our fixture.\nLove is our nature.\nLet's be greater than sin.\nLet's begin to love without restraint for we know, we may never live again,\nso no moment is ever in vain.\nOur mortality is a permanent stain on our brains' untrained capacity to live again.\n\nSometimes words are just placed to make the world relate to emotions that may or may not be there.\n\nI have been thinking about why I even really know of Him. What do I truly want from Him?\n\nIt's hard to know someone who cannot be known,\nOr to ask something from The One who created ALL things.\nIt's baffling to imagine where to actually begin.\n\nHe said that His word is eternal life.\nSo I think I will begin there:\nSo I prophetically know that I can do all things through Him.",
